A||||3||WisconsinGT||Need your advice||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||10-24-2000||09:19 PM||||My driver's side door has had it's better days. I am hearing wind noise with the windows up. So, I bought two door pins from Rodney Dickman. I also have a flat spot that is annoying when opening and closing the door. After viewing the area, I noticed that I have a rust problem which may be the cause to all of this. Anyway, could you view the photo I took and give me your opinion on this? <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1289573&a=9559574&p=31475305" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1289573&a=9559574&p=31475305</A>  Oh, how hard is it to get a drivers side door for an 88GT with power windows/mirrors/locks? Cost? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||10-24-2000||11:09 PM||||OUCH, that rust isn't going to help any that's for sure. As for the flat spot, from what I can see it's supposed to be there.It holds the door open at different distances. You might want to hit that roller with some lube though.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||10-25-2000||09:16 AM||||Lube the hole in the roller, not the actual roller itself.  Getting lube on the roller causes it to slip against the mating part instead of actually rolling on its shaft.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||10-25-2000||10:03 AM||||Wow. You need to replace the door frame. Find one in a local bone yard, strip the door skin off and replace it with your door skin. If your lucky, you'll find one equiped just like your door (power/manual locks and windows). While you have the door off, it's a snap to rebuild the hinges.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
